In programming, working with strings often involves checking string lengths and accessing specific character positions. Here is a reference for common string operations across a few standard programming languages:

### String Operations Reference

#### Python
```python
# Getting the length of a string
length = len(my_string)

# Accessing characters by index (0-based)
first_char = my_string[0]
last_char = my_string[-1]

# Slicing a string [start:stop:step]
substring = my_string[0:5]
reversed_string = my_string[::-1]

# String methods
lowercased = my_string.lower()
```

#### Java
```java
// Getting the length of a string
int length = myString.length();

// Accessing characters by index (0-based)
char firstChar = myString.charAt(0);
char lastChar = myString.charAt(length - 1);

// Extracting a substring (beginIndex, endIndex)
String sub = myString.substring(0, 5);

// String methods
String lowercased = myString.toLowerCase();
```

#### C++
```cpp
#include <string>

// Getting the length of a string
size_t length = myString.length(); // or myString.size()

// Accessing characters by index (0-based)
char firstChar = myString[0];       // or myString.at(0)
char lastChar = myString[length - 1];

// Extracting a substring (start_index, length)
std::string sub = myString.substr(0, 5);
```

